CURRENT AGREED ARCHITECTURE

1. Producer lifecycle

A producer attempt has one immutable DecisionID created once at source-wrapper decision creation time.

DecisionID format:

    <Producer>_<YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS>M<mmm>

Example:

    Case13APeakSell_20260808T163003M123

DecisionID is only a correlation identifier.

Do NOT parse time back out of DecisionID.

CreatedAt is the authoritative time.Time used for:
- 24-hour retention
- sorting
- expiry

ProducerEvent.Time is the time of the individual lifecycle event.

2. Core types

type ProducerStage string

const (
    ProducerStageProduced            ProducerStage = "produced"
    ProducerStagePending             ProducerStage = "pending"
    ProducerStageFilled              ProducerStage = "filled"
    ProducerStageCommitted           ProducerStage = "committed"
    ProducerStageCancelRequested     ProducerStage = "cancel_requested"
    ProducerStageEntryFailed         ProducerStage = "entry_failed"
    ProducerStageCleanupCancelled    ProducerStage = "cleanup_cancelled"
    ProducerStageCleanupCancelFailed ProducerStage = "cleanup_cancel_failed"
)

type ProducerEvent struct {
    Time      time.Time
    CreatedAt time.Time

    Producer EntryProducer
    Side     string
    Stage    ProducerStage

    DecisionID string
    OrderID    string

    Reason string

    ErrorCode       EntryProduceErrorCode
    Error           string
    CleanupRequired bool

    PnL float64
}

type ProducerAttempt struct {
    DecisionID string
    CreatedAt  time.Time

    Producer EntryProducer
    Side     string

    Events map[ProducerStage]ProducerEvent
}

type ProducerHistory struct {
    Attempts map[string]*ProducerAttempt
}

Trader owns:

    producerHistory map[EntryProducer]*ProducerHistory

Logical structure:

    producerHistory[producer]
        .Attempts[decisionID]
        .Events[stage]

3. Entry production flow already implemented

Source wrappers:

    startProducerBuyEntry()
    startProducerSellEntry()
    startCase3AReplacement()

create:

    CreatedAt
    DecisionID
    stage=produced

They call:

    produceEntry()

produceEntry() returns:

    (*PendingEntry, *ProducerAttempt, error)

produceEntry() collects:

    pending
or
    entry_failed

Entry helpers construct their own granular EntryProduceError at the exact point where the failure is known.

Higher layers must not reclassify those errors.

EntryProduceError:

type EntryProduceError struct {
    Code            EntryProduceErrorCode
    Producer        EntryProducer
    Side            string
    OrderID         string
    CleanupRequired bool
    Err             error
}

produceEntry() converts EntryProduceError → ProducerEvent but still propagates the structured error upward.

4. Cleanup handling already implemented

handleEntryProduceError(
    ctx,
    intent,
    attempt,
    err,
)

owns immediate exchange cleanup after entry production failure.

It may append:

    cleanup_cancelled

or:

    cleanup_cancel_failed

to the SAME ProducerAttempt / SAME DecisionID.

It does NOT write producerHistory.

5. Higher-level callers own recording attempts

Normal BUY/SELL higher-level caller is Step().

Case3A higher-level caller is closeLot() / Case3A retry flow.

Those higher-level callers record attempts using:

func (t *Trader) recordProducerAttemptLocked(
    attempt *ProducerAttempt,
)

This helper:

- requires t.mu already held
- performs only the mechanical map update
- does NOT perform retry policy
- does NOT perform cleanup
- does NOT persist state
- does NOT mutate trading behavior

It writes:

    producerHistory[attempt.Producer].
        Attempts[attempt.DecisionID] = attempt

6. Case3A behavior must remain unchanged

Case3A retry policy is handled above the source wrapper.

handleCase3AReplacementError() distinguishes:

Known retryable:
    EntryProduceErrPostOnlySubmit
    EntryProduceErrPersistState

Cleanup uncertain:
    EntryProduceErrCleanupCancel

Known validation/build/register failures:
    non-retryable

Unknown/new error codes:
    non-retryable by default
    log exact ErrorCode and Err
    classify deliberately later

Deferred retries are executed from PendingReplacementRetry in Step().

Every actual retry is a NEW ProducerAttempt with a NEW DecisionID.

7. Locking rule

Never call startCase3AReplacement()/produceEntry() while holding t.mu if the downstream path may acquire t.mu.

closeLot() has already been mutated to release t.mu before Case3A replacement entry production, then reacquire it, refresh local lot state, and record ProducerAttempt.

DO NOT undo this.

